      "side": 1,
      "message": "Only result.rc \u003d\u003d 0 is checked here, which confirms curl executed without crashing, but not that it actually returned a valid HTTP status code in stdout. If curl\u0027s -w \u0027%{http_code}\u0027 output is empty, truncated, or malformed for any reason, this will silently return bad data to the caller, which will then fail later with a confusing/misleading error.\n\nSuggest adding a format check before returning:\n\nShould Be Equal As Integers  ${result.rc}  0\n    ...  msg\u003dcurl failed (rc\u003d${result.rc}); unable to evaluate the LDAP user request.\n\nShould Match Regexp  ${result.stdout}  ^\\d{3}$\n...  msg\u003dcurl did not return a valid 3-digit HTTP status code. Got: \u0027${result.stdout}\u0027",
